INSERT INTO glossary (id,term,definition,plain_english,purpose_function,practical_application,category,related_terms,common_mistakes,scenario_contexts,achievement_id)
SELECT 'd46a7876-a047-5bad-8795-0d0d9703b45d','Piano boundary miking','A piano-miking technique using boundary (pressure-zone) microphones, capsules mounted flush against a large surface, typically taped to the underside of the raised lid or laid inside the case near the soundboard. Working at the boundary, the mic sums the direct and reflected sound in phase, avoiding the comb-filtering of a spaced mic while giving a close, consistent and often brighter, more percussive tone.','A boundary mic is a flat mic that sits right against a surface. On a piano it is taped to the underside of the raised lid or set inside. Sitting on the surface, it avoids the hollow, phasey sound of reflections and gives a close, punchy tone.','It exists to capture a close, phase-coherent piano sound in a compact, low-profile way, useful when a mic stand is impractical or when reflections off the lid would otherwise smear the tone.','An engineer tapes a boundary mic to the underside of the piano''s raised lid or inside the case, sets the lid to the desired angle, and gets a consistent, isolated piano sound with no stands in the sightline.','Piano miking',ARRAY['Boundary microphone','Comb filtering','Piano soundboard miking','Piano hammer emphasis','Phase cancellation']::text[],ARRAY['Mounting the boundary mic to a small or flimsy surface, so it no longer behaves as a true boundary and loses its low-end and phase benefit.','Expecting a natural, distant concert-piano tone; boundary miking inside the case sounds close and can be honky.','Taping the capsule poorly so it buzzes or rattles against the lid and adds noise to the recording.']::text[],ARRAY['Miking a grand on a live stage where mic stands are in the way or unsightly.','Getting a bright, present pop or rock piano from a grand with the lid down.','Recording piano in a small or reflective room where spaced mics would sound phasey.']::text[],'c1bd3df7-1ba9-416e-8ebd-538a91ac2517'
WHERE NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM glossary g WHERE g.id='d46a7876-a047-5bad-8795-0d0d9703b45d' OR regexp_replace(lower(g.term),'[^a-z0-9]','','g')=regexp_replace(lower('Piano boundary miking'),'[^a-z0-9]','','g'));
INSERT INTO glossary_topics (glossary_id,achievement_id,is_primary)
SELECT 'd46a7876-a047-5bad-8795-0d0d9703b45d','c1bd3df7-1ba9-416e-8ebd-538a91ac2517',true
WHERE NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM glossary_topics gt WHERE gt.glossary_id='d46a7876-a047-5bad-8795-0d0d9703b45d' AND gt.achievement_id='c1bd3df7-1ba9-416e-8ebd-538a91ac2517');
INSERT INTO glossary (id,term,definition,plain_english,purpose_function,practical_application,category,related_terms,common_mistakes,scenario_contexts,achievement_id)
SELECT '2f6848e4-f945-5ac0-8539-59f9a4084a59','Piano hammer emphasis','A piano-miking approach that positions or aims microphones near the hammers and the string strike point to emphasize the percussive attack of each note. Miking close over the hammers captures the transient click of felt striking the strings and extra brightness, giving an aggressive, present piano tone favored in pop and rock, at the expense of the rounder, more blended sound of mics placed farther back over the soundboard.','The hammers are the felt-covered parts that strike a piano''s strings. Aiming mics close to them brings out the sharp attack of each note. This gives a bright, punchy piano that cuts through a loud mix.','It exists to give a piano more attack and definition so it stays audible and rhythmic in dense arrangements, where a softer, distant sound would get buried.','An engineer moves the mics forward over the hammers and strike line of a grand, trading some warmth for extra bite so the piano cuts through a band mix.','Piano miking',ARRAY['Piano soundboard miking','Piano boundary miking','Transient','Close miking','Proximity effect']::text[],ARRAY['Placing the mics so close to the hammers that mechanical action noise and thumps dominate the tone.','Using hammer emphasis on a solo classical piece, where the sharp attack sounds harsh and unmusical.','Forgetting that lid position and mic height also shape attack, and blaming the mic choice alone.']::text[],ARRAY['Recording a driving pop or rock piano that must cut through guitars and drums.','Adding rhythmic bite to a piano comping part in a busy arrangement.','Reinforcing a stage piano where attack and clarity matter more than natural warmth.']::text[],'c1bd3df7-1ba9-416e-8ebd-538a91ac2517'
WHERE NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM glossary g WHERE g.id='2f6848e4-f945-5ac0-8539-59f9a4084a59' OR regexp_replace(lower(g.term),'[^a-z0-9]','','g')=regexp_replace(lower('Piano hammer emphasis'),'[^a-z0-9]','','g'));
INSERT INTO glossary_topics (glossary_id,achievement_id,is_primary)
SELECT '2f6848e4-f945-5ac0-8539-59f9a4084a59','c1bd3df7-1ba9-416e-8ebd-538a91ac2517',true
WHERE NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM glossary_topics gt WHERE gt.glossary_id='2f6848e4-f945-5ac0-8539-59f9a4084a59' AND gt.achievement_id='c1bd3df7-1ba9-416e-8ebd-538a91ac2517');
INSERT INTO glossary (id,term,definition,plain_english,purpose_function,practical_application,category,related_terms,common_mistakes,scenario_contexts,achievement_id)
SELECT 'e9008dd0-9529-5994-a5a1-09691591bd61','Piano soundboard miking','A piano-miking technique that places microphones at the soundboard, typically underneath a grand piano facing the board, or behind or against the soundboard of an upright, rather than over the strings and hammers. The soundboard radiates the instrument''s full, resonant body tone, so this position yields a warm, rounded sound with less hammer attack, and can improve isolation from other instruments on stage.','The soundboard is the large wooden panel that makes a piano''s sound resonate. Miking it, often from underneath a grand, captures a warm, full tone. It picks up less of the sharp hammer attack than mics over the strings.','It exists to capture the piano''s warm, resonant body and to isolate it from surrounding instruments, especially on loud stages where over-string mics would pick up too much spill.','A live engineer places a mic under the grand facing the soundboard to get a full, isolated piano sound with reduced bleed from the rest of the band.','Piano miking',ARRAY['Piano hammer emphasis','Piano boundary miking','Close miking','Proximity effect','Isolation']::text[],ARRAY['Expecting strong note attack from a soundboard mic; the position favors warmth and body over transient bite.','Placing the mic where the pedal mechanism or floor reflections add thumps and boominess.','Assuming under-lid and under-soundboard positions sound the same; the soundboard gives a rounder, less bright tone.']::text[],ARRAY['Miking a grand on a loud stage to reduce spill from drums and guitars.','Capturing a warm, full piano body tone for a ballad.','Adding a soundboard mic to blend with brighter over-string mics for a fuller sound.']::text[],'c1bd3df7-1ba9-416e-8ebd-538a91ac2517'
WHERE NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM glossary g WHERE g.id='e9008dd0-9529-5994-a5a1-09691591bd61' OR regexp_replace(lower(g.term),'[^a-z0-9]','','g')=regexp_replace(lower('Piano soundboard miking'),'[^a-z0-9]','','g'));
INSERT INTO glossary_topics (glossary_id,achievement_id,is_primary)
SELECT 'e9008dd0-9529-5994-a5a1-09691591bd61','c1bd3df7-1ba9-416e-8ebd-538a91ac2517',true
WHERE NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM glossary_topics gt WHERE gt.glossary_id='e9008dd0-9529-5994-a5a1-09691591bd61' AND gt.achievement_id='c1bd3df7-1ba9-416e-8ebd-538a91ac2517');
INSERT INTO glossary (id,term,definition,plain_english,purpose_function,practical_application,category,related_terms,common_mistakes,scenario_contexts,achievement_id)
SELECT 'aba36e70-9b11-5d12-959f-1296bdf00d40','Pick-attack isolation','A technique for capturing or emphasizing the transient click of a pick (plectrum) striking a string, distinct from the instrument''s sustained body tone. On acoustic or electric guitar and bass it is achieved by aiming a microphone near the picking hand and bridge, or by blending a bright direct or pickup signal, so the attack of each note stays articulate and defined in the mix.','When a pick hits a string, it makes a sharp clicking attack. This technique captures that click clearly, often with a mic near the picking hand. It makes each note''s start crisp so fast playing stays defined in a mix.','It exists to add articulation and definition so picked notes cut through and rhythms stay tight, especially for fast or busy parts that would otherwise sound mushy.','An engineer aims a mic toward the bridge and picking-hand area, or blends in a direct signal, to bring up pick attack, then balances it against a body or amp mic for clarity without harshness.','String miking',ARRAY['Transient','Direct injection','Close miking','Off-f-hole miking','3:1 rule']::text[],ARRAY['Aiming straight at the sound hole for more attack, which adds boom instead of the crisp pick click.','Over-emphasizing the pick attack until it sounds clicky and fatiguing and the note loses its body.','Blending a mic and a direct signal without checking phase, which can thin or hollow the tone.']::text[],ARRAY['Recording a fast picked acoustic part that must stay clear in a busy arrangement.','Adding definition to a bass direct signal so the pick attack cuts through a loud band.','Capturing tight, articulate rhythm guitar for a dense pop or rock mix.']::text[],'c1bd3df7-1ba9-416e-8ebd-538a91ac2517'
WHERE NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM glossary g WHERE g.id='aba36e70-9b11-5d12-959f-1296bdf00d40' OR regexp_replace(lower(g.term),'[^a-z0-9]','','g')=regexp_replace(lower('Pick-attack isolation'),'[^a-z0-9]','','g'));
INSERT INTO glossary_topics (glossary_id,achievement_id,is_primary)
SELECT 'aba36e70-9b11-5d12-959f-1296bdf00d40','c1bd3df7-1ba9-416e-8ebd-538a91ac2517',true
WHERE NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM glossary_topics gt WHERE gt.glossary_id='aba36e70-9b11-5d12-959f-1296bdf00d40' AND gt.achievement_id='c1bd3df7-1ba9-416e-8ebd-538a91ac2517');
INSERT INTO glossary (id,term,definition,plain_english,purpose_function,practical_application,category,related_terms,common_mistakes,scenario_contexts,achievement_id)
SELECT 'c75ee332-ada9-5d2d-9b91-9c680fc32dd7','Plosive shadowing','A vocal-recording technique that reduces plosive pops, the low-frequency thumps caused by bursts of air from consonants such as p and b striking the diaphragm, by placing the microphone outside the direct path of that airflow. Positioning the mic above, below or off to the side of the mouth, often combined with a pop filter and adequate distance, keeps the diaphragm in the shadow of the air blast while still capturing the voice.','Saying p and b sounds pushes a puff of air that thumps a mic and makes a pop. This technique keeps the mic out of that air path. Aiming it a bit above, below or to the side lets the puff miss it while still hearing the voice.','It exists to prevent plosive pops from overloading the mic and muddying a recording, without dulling the voice the way heavy filtering or a distant mic would.','An engineer angles a vocal mic slightly off the mouth or tilts it up or down, adds a pop filter a few inches out, and checks that hard p words no longer thump.','Vocal miking',ARRAY['Pop filter','Proximity effect','Close miking','Cardioid pattern','High-pass filter']::text[],ARRAY['Relying only on a low-cut filter to fix pops, which thins the voice instead of stopping the air blast at its source.','Placing the mic dead-center and close to the mouth, right in the plosive airflow, then fighting pops in the mix.','Moving so far off-axis that the tone dulls; the goal is out of the air path, not off the voice entirely.']::text[],ARRAY['Recording a close lead vocal where hard consonants keep popping the mic.','Tracking voiceover or podcast speech that must stay clean and pop-free.','Setting up a handheld or stand mic for a singer who works very close to the capsule.']::text[],'c1bd3df7-1ba9-416e-8ebd-538a91ac2517'
WHERE NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM glossary g WHERE g.id='c75ee332-ada9-5d2d-9b91-9c680fc32dd7' OR regexp_replace(lower(g.term),'[^a-z0-9]','','g')=regexp_replace(lower('Plosive shadowing'),'[^a-z0-9]','','g'));
